{"hash":"*","by":"stand-in planner","searches":0,"data":{"why":"A fridge cut open in the middle of a kitchen: it starts as an icebox (food and a block of ice), the ice melts, a frosting coil replaces it, the coil runs out, and a compressor with coils underneath closes the loop. The camera opens close on the ice and the food, stays mid on the fridge and its parts for the chain, and ends on the home view with the compressor humming and the door open.","story":{"title":"How a fridge works","hero":"a refrigerator","parts":["food","block of ice","cooling coil","compressor","coils underneath","pipes","door","shelves","light"],"ideas":[{"role":"hook","idea":"put food in a box with a block of ice and you already have a fridge"},{"role":"problem","idea":"the ice melts and drips onto the food"},{"role":"fix1","idea":"replace the ice with a coil of liquid that boils at minus 26 degrees, so the coil frosts over"},{"role":"problem2","idea":"once the liquid has boiled away the frost melts and the box warms up again"},{"role":"fix2","idea":"a compressor squeezes the gas back into a liquid and pumps it round, so the coil frosts again"},{"role":"name","idea":"this box with a coil, a compressor and pipes is a refrigerator"},{"role":"how","idea":"squeezing makes the gas hot, so the coils underneath shed that heat into the kitchen"},{"role":"fact","idea":"inside it holds your food at 4 degrees, where germs grow slowly"},{"role":"myth","idea":"the cold you feel is not blown in"},{"role":"mythFact","idea":"a fridge only moves heat out of the box"},{"role":"finish","idea":"a door, shelves and a light complete the fridge"},{"role":"congrats","idea":"calm end: the fridge hums with its door open and its light on"}],"chain":[{"problem":"problem","causedBy":"hook","shows":"the ice block shrinks and water drips onto the food","stakes":"the food gets wet and warm","size":3},{"problem":"problem2","causedBy":"fix1","shows":"the frost on the coil melts away and a thermometer climbs to 15 degrees","